.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-opc 1  "bhtune-opc "
.SH NAME
bhtune\-opc \- Low\-level OPC DA passthrough (diagnostics) via the opcda\-bridge gateway, bypassing the tuning engine entirely
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-opc\fR [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Low\-level OPC DA passthrough (diagnostics) via the opcda\-bridge gateway, bypassing the tuning engine entirely
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
How to print OPC diagnostic results
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-servers(1)
List the OPC DA servers registered on the bridge gateway\*(Aqs host
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-read(1)
Read one or more tags
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-write(1)
Write a value to one tag
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-browse(1)
Browse one bounded page of tags. Without a session, lists the root level
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-close(1)
Explicitly release a gateway browse session returned by `opc browse`
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-search(1)
Search the OPC DA namespace without downloading the whole tree
.TP
bhtune\-opc\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
